(text "24 V BUS (red): bench supply + -> F0 -> VM on every driver. Ground return (black): every driver GND -> bench supply -" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 205.74 106.68 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid bd167d14-6c0a-47cd-a650-c02865a670c2))
(text "NOTES\n1. Mega pins: STEP D22-27, DIR D30-35, EN D36-41 (LOW = driver on; 10k pull-ups keep drivers OFF while the Mega boots), encoders A0-A5, gripper PWM D9.\n2. TMC2209 standalone mode: UART mode: MS1/MS2 set each driver bus address (0-2), microstep is set over UART. CLK = GND selects the internal clock.\n3. Check pin names against the silkscreen of the TMC2209 modules you buy (vendors differ). Set phase current with the module trimmer before connecting the arm.\n4. TMC2209 VM max is about 29 V: 24 V only. Never plug or unplug a motor with 24 V present. Verify coil pairs with an ohmmeter.\n5. Modules sit in female headers on perfboard. Heatsink on every module, 40 mm fan over the row.\n6. All grounds common. Never connect 24 V or 6 V to the Mega 5 V pins." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 40.64 535.94 0) (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left top)) (uuid 6047d52d-c460-409a-87bf-0182a70607c4))
(text "BILL OF MATERIALS (all Amazon; prices are estimates, check the cart; full links in bom.csv)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 30.48 358.14 0) (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left top)) (uuid 12cf09ee-785b-4b94-9ea2-e9cd0572e1a5))
(text "Ref\nU1\nPS2\nU2\nPS1\nDRV1-DRV6\nM1-M3\nM4-M6\nM7\nU6\nENC1-ENC6\nF0-F2\nSW1\nK1\nC7, C20-C25\nC1-C6, C8\nR1-R6, R13, R21-R26, R31-R32\n-\n-\n-\n-\n-\n-\nTOTAL" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 30.48 363.22 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 45e9da0d-52fd-40a5-bd3b-1cc45b93ed47))
(text "Qty\n1\n1\n1\n1\n6\n3\n3\n1\n1\n6\n3\n1\n1\n7\n7\n15\n1\n1\n1\n1\n1\n1\n" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 60.96 363.22 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid bedd3dc9-1c93-422e-838e-0933ece8a4e8))
(text "Part\nRaspberry Pi 5 8GB\nOfficial Raspberry Pi 27 W USB-C supply\nArduino Mega 2560 R3\nLab bench supply, 24 V, 3 A limit\nBIGTREETECH TMC2209 V1.3 + heatsink\nSTEPPERONLINE Nema 17 17HS19-2004S1, 59 Ncm 2 A\nSTEPPERONLINE Nema 17 17HS08-1004S, 16 Ncm 1 A\nMG996R servo (gripper)\nXL4015 5 A buck module, set 6.0 V\nAS5600 magnetic encoder module + diametric magnet\nInline ATO fuse holder + fuses\nE-stop, 22 mm latching mushroom, 1 NC\n24 V 30 A relay, normally open, with socket\nElectrolytic 1000 uF 16 V (x1), 100 uF 35 V (x6)\nCeramic 100 nF\n1k (x9), 10k (x6) metal film 1/4 W\nDriver carrier: prototype board\n2.54 mm female headers (driver sockets)\n40 mm 5 V fan over driver row\nUSB-A to USB-B cable (Pi to Mega)\n18 AWG silicone wire (24 V, motors)\n22 AWG silicone wire (signals)\nNew purchases, estimate before tax and shipping" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 71.12 363.22 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 0aa98bb7-08d6-449c-9948-4cebed74f569))
